## Context

Child of tracker 0008 (split by raid f9e483: the ticket bundled five sign-off units over ~25 files). Read 0008's body and log for the up-front decisions: `Kind` is a `Literal`, `ACCEPTS` a `frozenset[str]`; one `DEFAULT_ORDER` constant for the cascade; no `detail_url` (no consumer found); contract as data plus a signature, no ABC/Protocol/base class.

Line endings: cli.py, config.py and sources crossref, hal, libgen, scihub, unpaywall, url are CRLF; keep each file's endings, no whole-file diffs.

## Actions
1. `src/doifetch/sources/contract.py`: frozen dataclasses `Request` (kind, identifier, target path) and
   `Result` (`status` Literal, `source`, `path`, `error`), `Fetch = Callable[[Request], Result]`, the
   contract rules in the module docstring (0008 Actions 1 and 3).
2. Each source module gains `NAME`, `ACCEPTS` and `fetch(req) -> Result` as a thin adapter over its
   legacy function, in the module itself, so later children edit only their own modules.
3. `cli.py` registry becomes `dict[str, Fetch]`; dispatch reads `ACCEPTS`, not string prefixes; the cascade
   order is one `DEFAULT_ORDER` constant.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Every source exposes `NAME`, `ACCEPTS`, `fetch`; no class in `sources/`; the type checker passes
- [ ] `cli.py` has no per-source special case
- [ ] Behaviour unchanged on the existing suite
